### AI-assistant session state ###
# Claude Code's own local/session state - not project source.
.claude/

# Point-in-time notes and reports generated during Claude-assisted work
# sessions (quality/security audits, release-readiness reports, etc.) - not
# meant to live in version control as the codebase moves on. Everything else
# under docs/ (requirements, personas, use cases, diagrams, ...) is real
# project documentation and stays tracked, as does CLAUDE.md.
docs/quality-baseline-*.md
docs/release-readiness-*.md


# Maintainer's local device-test feedback intake; formulated TODOs live in docs/TODO.md
tasks.txt

# Python bytecode cache (scripts/*.py, e.g. mobsfscan_check.py, mobsf_summary.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Project rule: after every newly built feature, a `current.apk` sits here for
# flashing (see CLAUDE.md, "Current APK"). Deliberately NOT tracked - it's a
# build output, changes with every feature, and would be 80 MB per commit.
current.apk


# Evidence from scripts/verify-alarm-survival.sh (device model, serial and raw
# dumpsys output of the maintainer's own phone - untracked on purpose, see the
# PII policy in CLAUDE.md). Only *.log was ignored before, which would have let
# any other artefact in that directory slip into a commit.
evidence/
